<a href="Uttar-Pradesh-Destinations/Ghaziabad.aspx"><strong>Ghaziabad Tour</strong></a>
<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Bahadurgarh.jpeg" alt="Bahadur garh, Ghaziabad tour" title="Bahadur garh, Ghaziabad tour" class="thumb alignright"  style="width:120px;height:100px;float:right" />
<p>The historical city Ghaziabad is gateway to Uttar Pradesh, hence is popular as Gateway of UP. The town shares it's boundary with Delhi. The town is hub of industries as well as an emerging hub for education of NCR.<a href="Uttar-Pradesh-Destinations/Ghaziabad.aspx">MORE...</a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<a href="Assam-Destinations/Guwahati.aspx"><strong>Guwahati Tour</strong></a>
<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Bhubaneshwari-temple-guwahati.jpeg" alt="Bhubaneshwari Temple, Guwahati tour" title="Bhubaneshwari Temple, Guwahati tour" class="thumb alignleft"  style="width:120px;height:100px;float:left" />
<p>Guwahati, the largest city in the green state of Assam is situated on the banks of the mighty river Brahmaputra. The name is the combination of two words: Guwa meaning areca nut and Hat meaning market. Guwahati or Gurahati is the gateway to the most exotic and fascinating north-eastern regions of India.<a href="Assam-Destinations/Guwahati.aspx">MORE...</a></p>
<br/>
<br/>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
